<!-- ── FAQ ── -->
<section id="faq" data-screen-label="08 FAQ">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="slabel">Section 07 · FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="sec-h">Questions we kept hearing.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Will my account get flagged or banned? <span class="faq-icn">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">pnv runs a real Chromium browser — not a script, not an API call. From the platform's perspective, it looks like a person using a browser, because it is. That said, aggressive automation on any platform carries risk. We recommend keeping task frequency within what a human would reasonably do. pnv is a personal automation tool — you decide the pace.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Which platforms does pnv support? <span class="faq-icn">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Any platform your browser can reach: X (Twitter), Threads, Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn, YouTube, and more. pnv doesn't use platform APIs — it uses the browser UI directly, so there are no API keys to manage and no rate limits from the platform side.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">How is this different from Buffer or Hootsuite? <span class="faq-icn">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Buffer and Hootsuite schedule posts. That's it. pnv automates any browser action — like, comment, follow, scrape analytics, DM, fill forms, extract data. If you can do it in a browser, pnv can do it on a schedule.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">How is this different from Phantombuster? <span class="faq-icn">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Phantombuster requires you to configure automation scripts and workflows. pnv records what you do and replays it. No setup, no templates, no maintenance when the platform UI changes — just redo the recording.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Can I manage multiple social media accounts? <span class="faq-icn">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes. Each browser profile has its own cookies, session, and login state. Create a profile per account. Run separate tasks per profile. Profiles are free and unlimited.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

